# OPTIONAL: put the backend behind HTTPS on a real domain with automatic certs.
#
# Why you'd want this: the APK hardcodes a backend URL. A domain like
# https://music.example.com never changes, so your app keeps working even if the
# server's IP changes — unlike a bare LAN IP. HTTPS also lets you drop the
# `usesCleartextTraffic` workaround later.
#
# Prereqs: a domain's A record pointing at your server, ports 80 + 443 open.
# Run Caddy (easiest as a second compose service, or the system package):
#   caddy run --config ./deploy/Caddyfile
#
# Replace music.example.com with your domain. Caddy fetches + renews TLS certs
# from Let's Encrypt automatically.
music.example.com {
    reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8000
}
